n      (is (= :yin.k/undecodable (:status st)))\n      (is (zero? @(:attaches d)) \"no stream was attached\")\n      (is (= [] (inbound w \"holder-a\")) \"no request was sent\"))))\n\n\n(deftest a-missing-authority-attachment-is-unsatisfied-test\n  (let [{:keys [sources]} (reader-source)\n27:     :yin.k/bound          its epoch binding, in the grant's transaction\n30:     :yin.k/reclaimed      its epoch change, in the lapse's transaction:\n31:                           one above the binding's epoch, or the same\n32:                           epoch at the bound, which exhausts the\n39:                           the same transaction: its lease and epoch\n62:      :max-epoch   m      ; the epoch bound, 2^52-1 unless lowered\n69:                       :yin.k/epoch e :dao.lease/lease l-or-nil\n75:                       :yin.k/epoch e :dao.space/t t\n94:   `fold-record` answers the next projection, or `{::defect d}` when the\n123:                 :dao.lease/holder :yin.k/epoch]\n126:                     :yin.k/epoch]\n131:                  :yin.k/epoch]\n169:  \"The projection of an empty ledger.  `max-epoch`, a lower epoch bound\n172:  ([arbitration max-epoch]\n174:    :max-epoch max-epoch\n196:(defn- argument-defect!\n198:  (throw (ex-info (str \"Ledger argument defect: \" (name d))\n199:                  {::defect d :fact fact})))\n205:   attribute outside it, is an argument defect and throws: nothing is\n210:      (argument-defect! :unknown-kind fact))\n212:      (argument-defect! :unpublished-attribute fact))\n230:(defn- defect!\n232:  (throw (ex-info (str \"Ledger defect: \" (name d)) (assoc data ::defect d))))\n253:                (defect! :malformed-fact {:fact avs}))\n261:      (defect! :unknown-target {:yin.k/target i})))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
